<h4 class="boldbyline">
Re: The Good Writer
</h4>

<p>
I think you have to have the links, the life experience that gives real understanding and empathy. The understanding and ability to seize the "I care about this because" element comes most eloquently if we can relate to the person, and the setting. I'm not a better person in the sense of being a goody two shoes, I'm more humane, compassionate and (at the very least) more tolerant. I've learned by being a writer, few things are all black or all white. Most things are shades of gray. <br />
<br />
 I remember vividly what it was like to be a 13-year-old and to pick up the paper and see my father's picture and have amazing and unbelievable details of our life revealed. I learned by reading the paper that my father had killed a man in a jail break. (Dad was a state trooper.) I think because of that, I'm sensitive to the fact a lot of people are not used to being the day's front page news. It doesn't change the facts, but it keeps me striving to be fair, and honest, and avoid sensationalism. <br />

</p>
<div class="posted">Posted by:


